<title>
Precautions for Diagnosing Trouble
</title>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
For diagnosing troubles of the adaptive cruise control system, follow the procedure in 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0AA124001">Adaptive Cruise Control System Check:Adaptive Cruise Control</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
DTC(s) of adaptive cruise control system is stored not only in RBS control module but also in ECM. When diagnosing, check both RBS control module and ECM for the DTC(s).
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check that component parts related to the vehicle posture such as tires, suspension, etc. are standard parts.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check that front bumper is standard parts and well installed.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check that millimeter wave radar is installed in the original position.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check that millimeter wave radar is in the following conditions.
</ptxt>
</item>
<list2 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Sticker, film, etc. are not affixed or paint is not adhered.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
There is no abrasion or adhesion of dirt, etc. on the surface.
</ptxt>
</item>
</list2>
<item>
<ptxt>
When checking RBS control module (1) for terminal voltage or waveform, connect service wires (3) between the control module and connector (2).
</ptxt>
<figure>
